{"id": "ep-rdj", "titulo_en": "Success, Perspective, and Where You Come From", "titulo_es": "El éxito, la perspectiva y de dónde vienes", "proveedor": "fish", "hosts": {"A": "Robert", "B": "Zendaya"}, "audio": "/podcasts/ep-rdj.mp3", "lineas": [{"s": "Robert", "a": 0, "b": 8.48, "es": "Sabes, la gente me pregunta por el éxito todo el tiempo, y honestamente, creo que nos han vendido una historia muy conveniente sobre eso.", "nota": "", "w": [["You", 0, 0.24], ["know,", 0.24, 0.72], ["people", 0.8, 1.28], ["ask", 1.28, 1.6], ["me", 1.6, 1.76], ["about", 1.76, 2], ["success", 2, 2.4], ["all", 2.4, 2.64], ["the", 2.64, 2.8], ["time,", 2.8, 3.04], ["and", 3.04, 3.36], ["honestly,", 3.36, 3.84], ["I", 3.84, 4.08], ["think", 4.08, 4.64], ["we've", 4.64, 5.12], ["been", 5.12, 5.2], ["sold", 5.2, 5.68], ["a", 5.68, 6.08], ["very", 6.08, 6.4], ["convenient", 6.4, 6.96], ["little", 6.96, 7.36], ["story", 7.36, 7.68], ["about", 7.68, 8], ["it.", 8, 8.48]]}, {"s": "Zendaya", "a": 8.72, "b": 16.565, "es": "Vale, necesito escuchar esto, porque cada vez que alguien me explica el éxito, suena como un póster de gimnasio, y la vida real jamás ha funcionado así.", "nota": "", "w": [["Okay,", 8.72, 9.28], ["I", 9.28, 9.36], ["need", 9.36, 9.52], ["to", 9.52, 9.6], ["hear", 9.6, 9.84], ["this,", 9.84, 10], ["because", 10, 10.24], ["every", 10.24, 10.48], ["time", 10.48, 10.64], ["someone", 10.64, 10.96], ["explains", 10.96, 11.36], ["success", 11.36, 11.76], ["to", 11.76, 11.92], ["me,", 11.92, 12.4], ["it", 12.4, 12.48], ["sounds", 12.48, 12.8], ["like", 12.8, 12.96], ["a", 12.96, 13.12], ["poster", 13.12, 13.44], ["in", 13.44, 13.6], ["a", 13.6, 13.68], ["gym,", 13.68, 14], ["and", 14.165, 14.325], ["real", 14.325, 14.645], ["life", 14.645, 14.885], ["has", 14.885, 15.045], ["never", 15.045, 15.285], ["once", 15.285, 15.605], ["worked", 15.605, 15.845], ["that", 15.845, 16.085], ["way.", 16.085, 16.565]]}, {"s": "Robert", "a": 16.565, "b": 27.285, "es": "Exacto. La historia dice: trabaja duro, mantente positivo, y el universo te lo devuelve. Pero nadie menciona la parte donde tu punto de partida importa, enormemente.", "nota": "", "w": [["Exactly.", 16.565, 17.525], ["The", 17.525, 17.765], ["story", 17.765, 18.165], ["says,", 18.165, 18.485], ["work", 18.485, 18.965], ["hard,", 18.965, 19.605], ["stay", 19.605, 19.925], ["positive,", 19.925, 20.405], ["and", 20.405, 20.725], ["the", 20.725, 20.885], ["universe", 20.885, 21.285], ["pays", 21.285, 21.605], ["you", 21.605, 21.765], ["back.", 21.765, 22.325], ["But", 22.725, 22.885], ["nobody", 22.885, 23.365], ["mentions", 23.365, 23.925], ["the", 23.925, 24.165], ["part", 24.165, 24.405], ["where", 24.405, 24.725], ["your", 24.725, 25.125], ["starting", 25.125, 25.525], ["line", 25.525, 25.845], ["matters,", 25.845, 26.485], ["enormously.", 26.485, 27.285]]}, {"s": "Zendaya", "a": 27.88, "b": 36.04, "es": "Cierto, porque de dónde vienes lo cambia todo. La ciudad en la que creciste, el dinero en casa, incluso cómo se hablaba del fracaso en tu mesa.", "nota": "", "w": [["Right,", 27.88, 28.28], ["because", 28.28, 28.44], ["where", 28.44, 28.76], ["you", 28.76, 28.92], ["come", 28.92, 29.08], ["from", 29.08, 29.24], ["changes", 29.24, 29.72], ["everything.", 29.72, 30.44], ["The", 30.76, 30.92], ["city", 30.92, 31.16], ["you", 31.16, 31.32], ["grew", 31.32, 31.48], ["up", 31.48, 31.64], ["in,", 31.64, 31.96], ["the", 31.96, 32.04], ["money", 32.04, 32.28], ["in", 32.28, 32.44], ["the", 32.44, 32.52], ["house,", 32.52, 33.08], ["even", 33.16, 33.4], ["the", 33.4, 33.56], ["way", 33.56, 33.72], ["people", 33.72, 33.96], ["talked", 33.96, 34.28], ["about", 34.28, 34.44], ["failure", 34.44, 34.84], ["at", 34.84, 35.08], ["your", 35.08, 35.24], ["dinner", 35.24, 35.48], ["table.", 35.48, 36.04]]}, {"s": "Robert", "a": 36.04, "b": 47.345, "es": "Ese último es enorme. Si el fracaso significaba vergüenza en tu familia, aprendes a esconderte. Si significaba información, aprendes a ajustarte. Mismo talento, vidas completamente distintas.", "nota": "", "w": [["That", 36.04, 36.52], ["last", 36.52, 36.84], ["one", 36.84, 37], ["is", 37, 37.24], ["huge.", 37.24, 37.8], ["If", 38.12, 38.36], ["failure", 38.36, 38.76], ["meant", 38.76, 39.16], ["shame", 39.16, 39.4], ["in", 39.4, 39.64], ["your", 39.64, 39.8], ["family,", 39.8, 40.28], ["you", 40.28, 40.36], ["learn", 40.36, 40.6], ["to", 40.6, 40.76], ["hide.", 40.76, 41], ["If", 41.505, 41.825], ["it", 41.825, 41.905], ["meant", 41.905, 42.145], ["information,", 42.145, 43.025], ["you", 43.105, 43.185], ["learn", 43.185, 43.505], ["to", 43.505, 43.665], ["adjust.", 43.665, 44.305], ["Same", 44.785, 45.105], ["talent,", 45.105, 45.825], ["completely", 45.825, 46.305], ["different", 46.305, 46.705], ["lives.", 46.705, 47.345]]}, {"s": "Zendaya", "a": 47.745, "b": 54.305, "es": "Y eso es perspectiva, en realidad. Dos personas pueden vivir el mismo año, una lo llama desastre, la otra lo llama una lección.", "nota": "", "w": [["And", 47.745, 47.985], ["that's", 47.985, 48.305], ["perspective,", 48.305, 49.105], ["really.", 49.105, 49.425], ["Two", 49.425, 49.745], ["people", 49.745, 50.065], ["can", 50.065, 50.305], ["live", 50.305, 50.545], ["the", 50.545, 50.705], ["same", 50.705, 50.945], ["year,", 50.945, 51.425], ["one", 51.425, 51.825], ["calls", 51.825, 52.065], ["it", 52.065, 52.225], ["a", 52.225, 52.385], ["disaster,", 52.385, 53.025], ["the", 53.025, 53.185], ["other", 53.185, 53.345], ["calls", 53.345, 53.585], ["it", 53.585, 53.665], ["an", 53.665, 53.905], ["education.", 53.905, 54.305]]}, {"s": "Robert", "a": 54.72, "b": 64.32, "es": "Así que quizás el éxito no es la casa, ni la cifra. Quizás es mirar tu propia historia, con honestidad, y aún así querer escribir la página siguiente.", "nota": "", "w": [["So", 54.72, 55.12], ["maybe", 55.12, 55.44], ["success", 55.44, 55.92], ["isn't", 55.92, 56.4], ["the", 56.4, 56.56], ["house,", 56.56, 57.28], ["or", 57.36, 57.6], ["the", 57.6, 57.84], ["number.", 57.84, 58.48], ["Maybe", 58.64, 58.96], ["it's", 58.96, 59.2], ["looking", 59.2, 59.6], ["at", 59.6, 59.76], ["your", 59.76, 60], ["own", 60, 60.24], ["story,", 60.24, 60.8], ["with", 60.8, 61.2], ["honesty,", 61.2, 61.84], ["and", 61.84, 62.16], ["still", 62.16, 62.64], ["wanting", 62.64, 62.96], ["to", 62.96, 63.12], ["write", 63.12, 63.28], ["the", 63.28, 63.44], ["next", 63.44, 63.68], ["page.", 63.68, 64.32]]}, {"s": "Zendaya", "a": 64.64, "b": 66.64, "es": "Eso sí lo pondría en un póster.", "nota": "", "w": [["That,", 64.64, 65.28], ["I", 65.44, 65.6], ["would", 65.6, 65.76], ["put", 65.76, 65.92], ["on", 65.92, 66.08], ["a", 66.08, 66.24], ["poster.", 66.24, 66.64]]}], "glosario": {"convenient": "conveniente, que le viene bien a alguien", "to be sold a story": "que te vendan un cuento", "poster": "póster, cartel", "gym": "gimnasio", "not once": "ni una sola vez", "to stay positive": "mantenerse positivo", "the universe pays you back": "el universo te lo devuelve", "to mention": "mencionar", "starting line": "línea de salida, punto de partida", "to matter": "importar", "enormously": "enormemente", "to grow up": "crecer, criarse", "failure": "fracaso", "dinner table": "la mesa, la sobremesa familiar", "huge": "enorme, gigante", "shame": "vergüenza", "to hide": "esconderse", "to adjust": "ajustarse, adaptarse", "talent": "talento", "perspective": "perspectiva, punto de vista", "disaster": "desastre", "an education": "una lección, un aprendizaje", "the number": "la cifra (el dinero, los seguidores)", "honesty": "honestidad", "still": "aun así, todavía", "the next page": "la página siguiente"}, "expresiones": [{"expresion": "to be sold a story", "linea_aprox": 1, "coach_intro": "Cuando te «venden un cuento» no te venden un producto: te venden una explicación cómoda de cómo funciona el mundo. Robert la usa para decir que la versión oficial del éxito (esfuérzate y llegarás) nos la colocaron sin que la pidiéramos. Fíjate en que va en pasiva, «we've been sold», porque lo importante no es quién te la vendió, sino que te la creíste.", "coach_ejemplo": "«We were sold the idea that working weekends makes you successful.» — «Nos vendieron la idea de que trabajar los fines de semana te hace exitoso.»", "coach_cierre": "¿Qué cuento sobre el éxito te vendieron a ti cuando eras chico?"}, {"expresion": "your starting line", "linea_aprox": 3, "coach_intro": "«Starting line» es la línea de salida de una carrera, y en inglés se usa constantemente como metáfora de dónde arrancas en la vida: tu familia, tu ciudad, tu dinero. Robert dice que «matters, enormously», y esa coma antes de «enormously» no es un adorno: obliga a la pausa que hace caer la palabra con peso.", "coach_ejemplo": "«We finished the same race, but we didn't start at the same line.» — «Terminamos la misma carrera, pero no salimos de la misma línea.»", "coach_cierre": "Si piensas en tu propia línea de salida, ¿qué te dieron y qué te tocó conseguir solo?"}, {"expresion": "I would put that on a poster", "linea_aprox": 8, "coach_intro": "Zendaya cierra con un chiste que solo funciona si escuchaste el principio: ella misma se había burlado de que el éxito «sounds like a poster in a gym». Al final admite que la frase de Robert sí merecería el póster. Es la forma inglesa de decir «esa sí me la apunto», devolviendo una imagen que ya estaba en la conversación.", "coach_ejemplo": "«'Rest is part of the work.' Honestly, I'd put that on a poster.» — «'Descansar es parte del trabajo.' La verdad, eso lo pondría en un póster.»", "coach_cierre": "¿Qué frase que te hayan dicho pondrías tú en un póster?"}], "onda": [1, 0.84, 0.069, 0.618, 0.972, 0.771, 0.535, 0.659, 0.651, 0.64, 0.78, 0.72, 0.683, 0.757, 0.306, 0.614, 0.793, 0.959, 0.784, 0.684, 0.86, 0.678, 0.834, 0.576, 0.7, 0.75, 0.725, 0.129, 0.238, 0.81, 1, 0.941, 0.631, 0.801, 0.732, 0.675, 0.549, 0.511, 0.509, 0.545, 0.347, 0.836, 0.537, 0.593, 0.585, 0.547, 0.141, 0.819, 0.664, 0.701, 0.675, 0.573, 0.473, 0.538, 0, 0.782, 0.845, 0.528, 0.787, 1, 1, 0